WEBVTT

00:01.335 --> 00:03.337
[♪ theme music playing]

00:29.112 --> 00:30.197
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

00:33.283 --> 00:34.826
CHARACTERS, EVENTS, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND PLACES IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

00:34.910 --> 00:36.203
ALL CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMALS
FILMED IN A SAFE ENVIRONMENT

00:37.663 --> 00:39.873
[Chan] I'm not someone
who will leave in three months,

00:39.957 --> 00:42.584
nor someone who might never come back.

00:42.668 --> 00:44.336
Ms. Song, I want to stay

00:44.419 --> 00:45.462
with you.

00:46.463 --> 00:48.840
No, Haran. So I'll tell you everything.

00:49.591 --> 00:53.011
But to tell you everything precisely,

00:53.095 --> 00:54.721
I need some time.

00:54.805 --> 00:55.847
It won't take long.

00:56.431 --> 00:59.142
I'll tell you everything honestly soon.

00:59.643 --> 01:01.603
So when I do,

01:02.354 --> 01:03.647
please listen to everything.

01:03.730 --> 01:05.524
-[♪ dramatic music playing]
-[breath trembling]

01:05.607 --> 01:07.109
What if you're not okay?

01:07.192 --> 01:08.735
What if something else happens?

01:08.819 --> 01:11.697
I've been okay, I'm okay now,
and I'll keep being okay.

01:11.780 --> 01:12.781
So…

01:14.366 --> 01:15.367
let's go see

01:18.287 --> 01:20.205
the cherry blossoms in spring.

01:21.081 --> 01:23.667
We'll have shaved ice in summer,

01:23.750 --> 01:25.919
see the autumn leaves in fall,

01:26.753 --> 01:27.963
and in winter…

01:29.798 --> 01:31.550
it would be fun to go snowboarding.

01:34.845 --> 01:35.846
[sighs heavily]

01:38.890 --> 01:40.684
EPISODE 10

01:40.767 --> 01:42.311
[♪ music continues]

01:45.480 --> 01:47.357
[Haran] I think you dropped your bracelet.

01:47.441 --> 01:48.442
[bracelet clinking]

01:48.525 --> 01:49.693
This is yours, right?

01:52.779 --> 01:55.490
Oh. Hey, crybaby Song Haran.

01:55.991 --> 01:57.034
[chuckles]

02:00.329 --> 02:02.164
[♪ music swells]

02:05.250 --> 02:07.169
[♪ music continues]

02:15.218 --> 02:17.763
-Let's go.
-Let me return her bracelet.

02:18.430 --> 02:20.974
[metallic clinking, clattering]

02:21.058 --> 02:24.019
-[♪ music fades]
-[exclaims] Oh, no. I'm sorry. Oh…

02:25.270 --> 02:27.689
-Get your stuff. I'll do this.
-[stutters]

02:29.983 --> 02:31.318
[Chan] I came to ask you for help.

02:31.401 --> 02:33.236
I really want to protect something,

02:33.320 --> 02:35.697
but to do that, I need my memories.

02:35.781 --> 02:36.782
[♪ tense music playing]

02:36.865 --> 02:38.867
It's okay. It breaks sometimes.

02:38.950 --> 02:41.411
I've been wearing it for a long time.

02:43.622 --> 02:44.706
[Chan] I'm sorry.

02:46.083 --> 02:48.543
I'm sorry, I'll get it repaired for you.

02:48.627 --> 02:51.296
It's really fine, Haran.

02:53.799 --> 02:54.800
Excuse me?

02:54.883 --> 02:57.094
Ah. Your name was written on the pen.

02:58.220 --> 02:59.471
That's a pretty name.

03:01.014 --> 03:04.101
-Let's go.
-He seems to be in quite a hurry.

03:04.184 --> 03:05.560
You can go. It's fine.

03:07.562 --> 03:09.106
[hesitates] I'm really sorry…

03:10.982 --> 03:12.275
Why are you so on edge?

03:13.985 --> 03:17.656
[stutters] No, wait. I'm sorry.
You should hurry home and get some rest.

03:17.739 --> 03:19.449
Did the doctor say you're okay?

03:20.117 --> 03:21.118
Yes, I'm fine.

03:21.618 --> 03:22.661
So let's go.

03:33.922 --> 03:35.924
[♪ music fades]

03:37.467 --> 03:40.554
If you feel dizzy or uncomfortable,
tell me straightaway.

03:45.642 --> 03:46.643
[sighs softly]

03:48.562 --> 03:49.563
Sir.

03:50.063 --> 03:52.441
I'm sorry, but can you pull over nearby?

03:53.608 --> 03:55.277
Shouldn't you get some rest?

03:55.777 --> 03:56.862
I'm totally fine.

03:58.155 --> 04:01.158
Oh? There's a look of doubt on your face.

04:02.117 --> 04:05.287
[sighs heavily] Then I'll do 100 push-ups!

04:05.370 --> 04:06.371
[exclaims]

04:06.455 --> 04:08.331
All right, fine. I believe you.

04:08.415 --> 04:12.294
I feel like we'll just feel down
and regret it if we go home now.

04:12.794 --> 04:13.795
So…

04:13.879 --> 04:15.589
[♪ pleasant music playing]

04:15.672 --> 04:19.426
let's begin Seonu Chan's
birthday gift ceremony.

04:22.429 --> 04:24.139
That's my present, right?

04:25.015 --> 04:26.349
This…

04:26.433 --> 04:27.684
[Chan] Oh… Let me guess.

04:28.268 --> 04:31.062
Mmm… It's clothes.

04:31.772 --> 04:35.192
A cardigan you designed yourself.

04:35.817 --> 04:37.486
How did you know?

04:37.569 --> 04:38.945
I prepared this in secret.

04:39.029 --> 04:40.822
It was obvious.

04:40.906 --> 04:42.032
It was?

04:43.158 --> 04:45.202
Oh. I see…

04:46.578 --> 04:49.331
-Hang on. Just give me five minutes.
-[stutters]

04:51.208 --> 04:54.795
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

04:54.878 --> 04:57.464
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

04:57.547 --> 05:00.926
♪ Happy birthday, dear Seonu Chan ♪

05:01.009 --> 05:03.094
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

05:03.178 --> 05:04.513
[cheers]

05:04.596 --> 05:05.972
[exclaims] Wait.

05:06.056 --> 05:07.891
You should still make a wish

05:07.974 --> 05:10.811
even if it's just a humble
convenience store cake.

05:10.894 --> 05:12.562
Then make a wish with me.

05:22.322 --> 05:23.365
[inhales]

05:25.075 --> 05:26.993
Wow! [laughs]

05:27.077 --> 05:28.328
What did you wish for?

05:28.912 --> 05:31.665
It's a secret.
If I share it, it won't come true.

05:31.748 --> 05:33.208
Right.

05:33.291 --> 05:35.085
-[Chan clears throat]
-Then…

05:35.168 --> 05:37.838
I'll give you your birthday present now.

05:37.921 --> 05:40.257
-Happy birthday.
-Oh. Can I open it right now?

05:41.967 --> 05:43.510
[♪ pleasant song playing]

05:44.469 --> 05:45.762
[Chan exclaims excitedly]

05:48.181 --> 05:49.432
Huh?

05:49.516 --> 05:52.394
I didn't know about this.

05:52.477 --> 05:54.521
[exclaims] At least
I kept one thing a secret.

05:55.564 --> 05:56.606
[chuckles softly]

05:57.107 --> 05:58.358
I'm glad I was born.

06:00.110 --> 06:02.320
Song Haran wished me happy birthday.

06:04.030 --> 06:07.075
[inhales sharply, yells] Everybody!
Song Haran wished me happy birthday!

06:07.993 --> 06:09.786
[stutters] Are you crazy?

06:09.870 --> 06:11.037
-[Haran chuckles softly]
-[Chan inhales sharply]

06:11.121 --> 06:14.833
I'll wear this every day,
in spring, summer, fall, and winter.

06:14.916 --> 06:16.918
I'll wear this to bed, too.

06:17.002 --> 06:20.714
-Ah. And even when I'm showering.
-[Haran chuckles]

06:21.590 --> 06:24.968
I wanted to do more for you
since it's our first birthday together.

06:28.346 --> 06:29.890
Since you seem upset,

06:30.599 --> 06:31.600
how about a date tomorrow?

06:31.683 --> 06:34.603
We can watch a movie,
have a nice meal, hold hands,

06:34.686 --> 06:36.938
and take a walk while we chat.

06:37.022 --> 06:38.690
We'll do what other couples do.

06:39.774 --> 06:42.360
You should just rest. I'm worried.

06:42.944 --> 06:46.489
[sighs dejectedly] You leave me
no choice, then. I should do push-ups…

06:46.573 --> 06:49.492
-[exclaims] All right. Let's go on a date.
-[clears throat]

06:49.576 --> 06:50.827
[scoffs]

06:50.910 --> 06:55.665
But can you sing that part again?

06:56.541 --> 06:57.792
The…

06:57.876 --> 07:00.754
"dear Seonu Chan" part.

07:03.381 --> 07:05.925
I'll make your birthday
even more special next year.

07:06.009 --> 07:09.262
I'm going to use that trial
for the rest of my life.

07:13.141 --> 07:14.351
[chuckles softly]

07:14.434 --> 07:15.435
So…

07:16.936 --> 07:18.688
stay healthy, okay?

07:26.863 --> 07:28.323
I will.

07:29.449 --> 07:30.575
Besides,

07:31.159 --> 07:34.079
my mind's filled with you, Haran,

07:35.372 --> 07:38.041
so a tiny fragment in my brain…

07:38.958 --> 07:41.002
[exclaims boastfully] won't affect me.

07:51.346 --> 07:53.598
[♪ song continues]

07:55.934 --> 07:57.102
Sir?

07:57.185 --> 07:58.478
Just a moment.

08:10.407 --> 08:12.409
[♪ song fades]

08:12.492 --> 08:13.827
What?

08:14.536 --> 08:15.620
Why are we…

08:17.664 --> 08:19.833
We were in Chuncheon earlier…

08:24.546 --> 08:25.755
Manjae.

08:27.215 --> 08:29.592
We're here. Let's get off.

08:38.309 --> 08:39.561
[breath trembling]

08:41.563 --> 08:42.814
[Manjae] How long has it been?

08:43.440 --> 08:44.691
Where were you planning

08:46.151 --> 08:47.819
to disappear off to alone?

08:48.737 --> 08:49.821
[Nana] Manjae.

08:51.614 --> 08:52.699
What do I do?

08:53.575 --> 08:54.826
[♪ emotional music playing]

08:54.909 --> 08:56.244
What do I do about the kids?

09:00.749 --> 09:01.750
I want

09:02.834 --> 09:05.128
to stay with them longer.

09:07.964 --> 09:10.759
I want to stay with you longer, too.

09:12.677 --> 09:14.554
But what if I forget everything?

09:16.765 --> 09:19.267
[voice shaking] If I end up
forgetting you and the kids…

09:22.353 --> 09:23.563
[sobs]

09:23.646 --> 09:25.940
and everything else…

09:29.235 --> 09:30.361
I'm scared. [sniffles]

09:31.154 --> 09:32.697
[sobbing] I'm terrified.

09:34.783 --> 09:36.534
[Nana continues sobbing]

09:38.703 --> 09:39.704
[Manjae] It's all right.

09:40.330 --> 09:41.748
Everything will be okay.

09:42.874 --> 09:46.044
You can let it all out with me.

09:48.004 --> 09:49.005
Don't worry.

09:49.714 --> 09:50.840
I will never

09:51.716 --> 09:52.967
let you be alone.

09:54.803 --> 09:55.970
Never.

09:56.054 --> 09:58.223
[Nana crying]

10:05.730 --> 10:07.732
[♪ music fades]

10:14.447 --> 10:16.991
[inhales sharply] There's one missing.

10:23.748 --> 10:24.749
Huh?

10:24.833 --> 10:27.043
[metallic clinking, clattering]

10:28.461 --> 10:31.256
[sighs wearily] I took one of her charms.

10:31.840 --> 10:33.216
How do I get this back to her?

10:37.554 --> 10:40.140
[doctor] The shrapnel's still lodged deep
in the temporal bone.

10:41.432 --> 10:43.101
[sighs heavily]

10:43.184 --> 10:45.562
[♪ melancholic music playing]

10:52.902 --> 10:54.112
It's really fine,

10:54.696 --> 10:55.697
Haran.

11:05.540 --> 11:06.749
[Haran] What did you wish for?

11:07.709 --> 11:10.170
[Chan] I won't wish for anything else
for the rest of my life.

11:11.087 --> 11:13.298
Please just let me stay with this person

11:13.381 --> 11:15.800
who let me live again,

11:15.884 --> 11:19.345
through every tear and every smile.

11:19.888 --> 11:22.640
I'm going to use that trial
for the rest of my life.

11:23.183 --> 11:25.059
[Chan] Just allow me this one thing.

11:25.977 --> 11:28.062
Let me keep staying by her side.

11:41.659 --> 11:42.952
[sighs softly]

11:48.208 --> 11:53.671
My birthday, the day I decided
to explain everything,

11:54.422 --> 11:55.840
despite the gaps.

11:58.176 --> 12:00.178
[♪ music swells]

12:12.857 --> 12:14.776
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

12:15.485 --> 12:17.487
[♪ music fades]

12:17.570 --> 12:18.655
[Haran sighs]

12:18.738 --> 12:20.531
PETROUS PART OF THE TEMPORAL BONE

12:22.325 --> 12:24.911
-[knock on door]
-[Hayeong] Your sister's coming in.

12:26.412 --> 12:27.664
What?

12:27.747 --> 12:29.916
Are you applying for medical school, too?

12:29.999 --> 12:31.334
I was just looking up something.

12:31.417 --> 12:32.502
Is Grandma still sleeping?

12:32.585 --> 12:36.464
Yeah, it's the first time.
She never slept in, even on the weekends.

12:36.547 --> 12:39.300
[sighs] Is she tired
after her trip to Chuncheon?

12:39.926 --> 12:41.261
But what are those books for?

12:41.344 --> 12:44.555
I just thought I'd work
to get my mind off things.

12:44.639 --> 12:48.184
[gasps] Do you have the pigment book?
It wasn't in Grandma's study.

12:48.268 --> 12:51.020
It's probably in the attic. Hmm…

12:52.021 --> 12:53.856
Why are your eyes puffy? Did you cry?

12:54.732 --> 12:56.192
Huh? [chuckles]

12:56.276 --> 12:58.736
[stutters] Of course not.
I just slept well.

12:58.820 --> 13:00.822
Just go and find that book for me.

13:03.074 --> 13:04.200
[in English] Thank you.

13:15.336 --> 13:16.963
[Chan in Korean] You can overcome it.

13:18.047 --> 13:20.133
You'll be able to escape on your own.

13:20.925 --> 13:22.343
I wanted to show you, too.

13:22.427 --> 13:24.429
[♪ light-hearted music playing]

13:31.477 --> 13:34.522
What are you doing?
Why did you pull up your sleeves?

13:34.605 --> 13:36.524
I want to clear out some stuff.

13:36.607 --> 13:37.900
Like a spring deep clean.

13:37.984 --> 13:41.487
Get your head together.
It's the middle of winter.

13:42.530 --> 13:45.366
No, it's spring. [chuckles softly]

13:51.205 --> 13:53.750
I don't think I'll wear this.

13:55.835 --> 13:57.045
And this…

14:09.265 --> 14:11.142
-I'm heading out.
-Wait.

14:11.726 --> 14:13.519
-[in English] You've got mail.
-Oh?

14:13.603 --> 14:16.481
[in Korean] He must have sent a letter
since it's so hard to reach you.

14:16.564 --> 14:19.108
That poor Kang Hyeokchan.

14:19.192 --> 14:20.693
-See you later.
-Huh?

14:20.777 --> 14:22.862
-[cellphone vibrating]
-You're right. Oh…

14:24.322 --> 14:25.323
Yes?

14:25.865 --> 14:27.533
I'll be there right away.

14:28.534 --> 14:29.535
[sighs softly]

14:35.666 --> 14:37.668
[♪ sentimental music playing]

14:38.294 --> 14:41.255
[Hyeokchan] Haran, you must still be busy.

14:41.339 --> 14:44.634
It's already been a month
since I came to Boston.

14:44.717 --> 14:46.886
Everything still feels unfamiliar to me.

14:46.969 --> 14:50.640
I miss you, but it's hard to hear
your voice because of the time difference.

14:50.723 --> 14:52.892
I've been thinking
about a way to communicate.

14:52.975 --> 14:54.811
Can you use a messenger at work?

14:54.894 --> 14:55.937
Tell me if you can.

14:56.604 --> 14:57.939
Ah. Let me tell you something cool.

14:58.523 --> 15:00.733
My dorm roommate is Korean,

15:00.817 --> 15:02.276
and his name's Chan, too.

15:02.360 --> 15:03.528
[chuckles] Isn't that funny?

15:04.195 --> 15:06.572
But I think it'll be hard
to get close to him.

15:06.656 --> 15:08.741
He seems a bit closed off.

15:09.325 --> 15:11.077
I miss you so much, Haran.

15:11.160 --> 15:13.246
I'll come see you during summer break.

15:13.329 --> 15:15.414
Take care. I love you.

15:15.957 --> 15:16.958
[sighs softly]

15:17.834 --> 15:18.835
[cellphone vibrates]

15:20.795 --> 15:23.422
[Chan] I booked the movie tickets.
I'll see you at 5:00 p.m.

15:23.506 --> 15:25.466
Oh. I should get ready.

15:36.310 --> 15:38.312
-[♪ music fades]
-[Manjae exclaims]

15:39.647 --> 15:40.773
[Chan] Mr. Park.

15:40.857 --> 15:43.776
I might come home pretty late tonight.

15:46.612 --> 15:48.406
All right.

15:48.489 --> 15:51.242
Talk it out with Haran.

15:51.325 --> 15:55.329
If you're sincere,
I'm sure she'll understand.

16:00.126 --> 16:02.170
-All right. I will.
-Okay.

16:11.721 --> 16:13.806
[indistinct chatter]

16:15.016 --> 16:16.559
They must be in the corner.

16:16.642 --> 16:19.812
[groans] This is broken.
It won't charge. [tuts]

16:23.774 --> 16:25.776
[♪ suspenseful music plays]

16:27.695 --> 16:30.114
[hesitates] Do you have time
after the movie?

16:31.449 --> 16:33.367
There's something I have to tell you.

16:34.368 --> 16:37.622
I'll tell you everything honestly soon.

16:39.582 --> 16:40.791
All right.

16:42.543 --> 16:44.921
Oh? I forgot the other popcorn.

16:45.004 --> 16:46.631
I'll go get it.

16:46.714 --> 16:49.050
-Just wait here.
-I'll wait inside, then.

16:50.259 --> 16:51.552
[crackles]

16:52.929 --> 16:55.139
-[♪ tense music playing]
-[fire crackling]

16:57.350 --> 17:00.019
[breathes deeply]

17:01.604 --> 17:03.606
-[staff 1] Sorry about that.
-It's okay.

17:04.106 --> 17:05.107
Thank you.

17:06.984 --> 17:08.986
[fire alarm blaring]

17:09.070 --> 17:11.030
-Is it a false alarm?
-What do we do?

17:11.113 --> 17:13.699
[staff 2] Please follow the instructions
and evacuate immediately.

17:14.325 --> 17:15.326
Please don't push.

17:15.409 --> 17:16.452
[Chan] Song Haran.

17:17.787 --> 17:18.913
Please go downstairs.

17:19.747 --> 17:21.249
Don't push!

17:21.332 --> 17:22.625
[♪ music continues]

17:25.962 --> 17:27.672
[staff 3] Evacuate immediately.

17:29.423 --> 17:31.050
You shouldn't go inside.

17:31.133 --> 17:32.134
Sorry!

17:32.218 --> 17:33.344
-Sir!
-Song Haran!

17:34.595 --> 17:35.805
-Song Haran!
-[loud thud]

17:35.888 --> 17:37.515
[high-pitched ringing]

17:41.185 --> 17:42.395
[loud thud]

17:43.229 --> 17:44.480
[groans, winces]

17:45.648 --> 17:47.108
Stop it!

17:47.942 --> 17:49.235
[groans]

17:51.070 --> 17:52.113
[groans]

17:53.239 --> 17:55.241
[high-pitched ringing]

17:56.242 --> 17:57.243
[grunts]

17:59.787 --> 18:00.997
[Haran] Seonu Chan!

18:03.541 --> 18:05.501
Seonu Chan! [exhales]

18:06.002 --> 18:07.003
[Chan] I'll tell you everything.

18:07.086 --> 18:10.256
I'll tell you about the scars on my body.

18:10.339 --> 18:12.550
I don't do well in noisy places.

18:14.218 --> 18:16.304
[Haran] Seonu Chan! Where are you?

18:19.015 --> 18:20.766
[coughs, exclaims]

18:21.267 --> 18:23.019
-[Chan grunts]
-[gasps softly]

18:23.102 --> 18:25.271
[exclaims worriedly] Where were you?

18:25.354 --> 18:26.647
I couldn't see you outside,

18:26.731 --> 18:28.649
-so I thought you'd gone inside…
-I'm okay.

18:29.317 --> 18:32.069
[pants] I'm so relieved nothing happened.

18:32.653 --> 18:33.654
[Haran exclaims]

18:34.238 --> 18:35.448
[breathing heavily]

18:36.616 --> 18:37.825
It's okay.

18:38.576 --> 18:40.161
Let's go to the hospital
and get you checked.

18:40.244 --> 18:42.330
[Chan] I'll get a checkup soon.

18:42.830 --> 18:44.457
[breathing heavily] Don't worry.

18:45.666 --> 18:47.543
I'll be completely fine.

18:49.503 --> 18:51.505
[♪ music fades]

18:55.968 --> 18:57.219
[sighs]

18:57.303 --> 18:59.221
MEDICAL CHECKUP

18:59.305 --> 19:00.514
[door opens, closes]

19:02.642 --> 19:03.893
Grandma.

19:03.976 --> 19:06.103
What is it, Haran? Is something wrong?

19:11.150 --> 19:12.193
What do I do, Grandma?

19:12.276 --> 19:13.486
[♪ mellow music playing]

19:13.569 --> 19:15.696
He's not well.

19:16.906 --> 19:18.783
He keeps collapsing,

19:19.784 --> 19:21.869
and there's something lodged in his head.

19:22.662 --> 19:25.164
He says he's okay,
but he doesn't seem okay at all.

19:26.290 --> 19:28.918
[sighs] What do I do
if something happens to him?

19:30.169 --> 19:32.046
[Chan] I may not be

19:32.129 --> 19:35.883
as good for her as you believe.

19:42.807 --> 19:44.475
He's not keeping it from you.

19:45.184 --> 19:46.352
He probably can't

19:47.144 --> 19:48.145
because he's scared.

19:48.813 --> 19:51.399
He probably doesn't want
to burden you with his pain

19:52.066 --> 19:53.442
because it would hurt you.

19:53.526 --> 19:54.652
He cares more

19:55.486 --> 19:57.863
about protecting you than his own pain.

19:57.947 --> 19:59.990
But I want to protect him.

20:01.158 --> 20:03.327
I don't want him to go through it alone.

20:04.578 --> 20:06.956
But there's nothing I can do for him.

20:07.039 --> 20:08.749
Just stay by his side.

20:09.458 --> 20:13.379
People can stay strong
even with just one person by their side.

20:13.921 --> 20:14.964
Trust me, I know.

20:16.090 --> 20:18.676
So don't worry too much.

20:18.759 --> 20:21.637
I'm sure you'll find a way.

20:28.769 --> 20:29.770
[♪ music fades]

20:29.854 --> 20:31.021
[Chan sighs]

20:38.279 --> 20:39.280
Waste container…

20:39.905 --> 20:41.073
Kang Hyeokchan…

20:41.657 --> 20:42.700
Lab…

20:43.451 --> 20:44.618
Cha Sujin…

20:44.702 --> 20:46.162
-[♪ suspenseful music playing]
-[loud thud]

20:46.245 --> 20:47.288
[groans, winces]

20:47.371 --> 20:48.497
Stop it!

20:49.165 --> 20:50.332
And me…

20:51.834 --> 20:53.586
Was that day…

20:56.005 --> 20:57.173
[explosion]

20:57.757 --> 21:00.509
[Chan]
"Volatile reagent container fractured…"

21:00.593 --> 21:02.219
"Self-reactive event

21:02.303 --> 21:05.097
triggered by careless handling
of reagents."

21:05.598 --> 21:09.059
"The cause has not been
conclusively determined."

21:09.143 --> 21:10.144
No, there's nothing.

21:10.227 --> 21:11.771
I said I don't know!

21:11.854 --> 21:13.564
[sighs heavily]

21:13.647 --> 21:17.443
What is she trying to hide?

21:19.820 --> 21:20.946
[cellphone vibrates]

21:25.242 --> 21:27.077
[Haran] Don't do anything tomorrow

21:27.161 --> 21:28.996
and get plenty of rest.

21:29.079 --> 21:30.873
I'll always be by your side.

21:38.672 --> 21:42.301
MY BIRTHDAY, THE DAY I DECIDED
TO EXPLAIN EVERYTHING, DESPITE THE GAPS

21:45.262 --> 21:47.807
NEXT TO THE CONTAINER: KANG HYEOKCHAN
IN THE LAB: CHA SUJIN

21:51.185 --> 21:53.646
[groans, inhales deeply]

21:53.729 --> 21:55.731
[exhales heavily]

21:58.651 --> 21:59.652
[♪ music fades]

21:59.735 --> 22:01.737
12-WEEK REHABILITATION PLAN

22:02.279 --> 22:04.490
Ah. It's tomorrow.

22:05.074 --> 22:09.286
But, Mr. Park, when should we tell
Hadam and her sisters?

22:09.370 --> 22:10.788
Yougyum!

22:10.871 --> 22:12.248
Hey, Dad!

22:12.331 --> 22:13.415
Really? Okay.

22:13.499 --> 22:14.959
Is it your dad?

22:15.042 --> 22:16.710
-Let me say hi.
-Okay, Dad.

22:17.336 --> 22:19.839
-[line disconnects]
-I said I wanted to say hi.

22:20.881 --> 22:22.591
Oh, I didn't hear you.

22:23.634 --> 22:25.427
-Sorry.
-Gosh.

22:26.804 --> 22:28.806
Ta-da. It's pumpkin porridge.

22:28.889 --> 22:32.768
It's rich in beta-carotene and vitamin A,
so it'll help with the inflammation.

22:33.352 --> 22:34.687
Make sure to eat everything.

22:43.612 --> 22:45.489
-Hadam.
-Yes?

22:46.073 --> 22:48.242
You know I like you so, so much, right?

22:48.325 --> 22:50.452
You helped me stay strong
when I was in pain.

22:51.203 --> 22:53.539
If you ever have a hard time someday,

22:53.622 --> 22:57.126
I'll do the same for you
so that you stay strong.

22:57.209 --> 22:59.253
[chuckles softly] Sure.

22:59.336 --> 23:01.964
But that's not going to happen.

23:02.047 --> 23:04.592
Once you're better,
I'll have nothing but happy days ahead.

23:04.675 --> 23:06.010
[both chuckle softly]

23:16.270 --> 23:17.771
[♪ mellow music playing]

23:17.855 --> 23:19.023
[sighs softly]

23:24.361 --> 23:25.529
[chuckles softly]

23:27.573 --> 23:28.657
Hi.

23:28.741 --> 23:31.201
-Did you have a good weekend?
-Yes.

23:31.285 --> 23:33.203
I'm on my way to meet Mr. Chae.

23:33.287 --> 23:36.206
He sent me files on the material,
but they kept getting corrupted,

23:36.290 --> 23:37.666
so he's bringing them in person.

23:37.750 --> 23:39.501
He must have something to cover nearby.

23:40.586 --> 23:42.421
That's quite a coincidence.

23:42.504 --> 23:43.631
[chuckles softly]

23:45.424 --> 23:48.969
Ah. I was checking the sample dye
from the color team.

23:49.053 --> 23:50.512
I guess it wasn't dry yet.

23:51.555 --> 23:53.223
I'll get going, then.

23:55.517 --> 23:58.562
[sighs] I felt so awkward
I ended up rambling.

24:07.947 --> 24:09.949
[♪ music ends]

24:10.032 --> 24:12.743
Um… These are the colors
that Ms. Kim directed.

24:12.826 --> 24:15.496
[inhales sharply]
Then this would be the most similar,

24:15.579 --> 24:18.248
but it might look muted on the fabric.

24:18.332 --> 24:19.375
[Seunggyu] I think so, too.

24:19.458 --> 24:21.377
We should try mixing the colors again.

24:21.460 --> 24:24.338
Then let's apply the feedback
and submit a report for now.

24:24.421 --> 24:26.423
-[Raemee] Okay.
-[Pureum sniffs]

24:26.507 --> 24:27.633
Coffee?

24:27.716 --> 24:29.343
All right, everyone.

24:29.426 --> 24:31.303
Fresh coffee.

24:31.387 --> 24:33.180
-Mr. Park.
-Hello.

24:33.263 --> 24:34.431
What brings you here?

24:34.515 --> 24:36.392
I got a new batch of beans.

24:36.475 --> 24:37.643
Gosh.

24:37.726 --> 24:41.855
So I thought I'd deliver some
to my regular customers.

24:42.523 --> 24:44.191
[Sol and Raemee exclaim] Thank you.

24:44.274 --> 24:46.527
-[Manjae] No problem.
-I'm taking this one.

24:46.610 --> 24:48.237
It's totally my style.

24:48.320 --> 24:49.863
Oh, I'm sorry.

24:49.947 --> 24:53.158
-This is reserved for someone else.
-[Raemee chuckles awkwardly]

24:53.242 --> 24:55.035
-Take this.
-Okay.

24:55.119 --> 24:56.328
-[chuckles awkwardly]
-[Manjae chuckles]

24:56.412 --> 24:58.622
Too bad. Ribbons are my signature.

24:58.706 --> 25:00.499
[Sol and Raemee laugh]

25:01.083 --> 25:04.378
You brought coffee for everyone
since it'll be too obvious, right?

25:04.461 --> 25:05.713
-[Manjae] Oh…
-[Haran chuckles]

25:05.796 --> 25:07.548
-Could you tell?
-Yes.

25:07.631 --> 25:09.383
[both chuckle]

25:10.009 --> 25:11.593
How was your trip to Chuncheon?

25:11.677 --> 25:13.887
Grandma was so excited to go.

25:13.971 --> 25:16.640
Uh… Of course.

25:16.724 --> 25:17.808
We had a great time.

25:19.226 --> 25:21.645
By the way, is Mr. Seonu okay?

25:21.729 --> 25:23.731
I didn't call
since I didn't want to bother him.

25:23.814 --> 25:26.442
What? Did something happen?

25:27.026 --> 25:30.279
He clearly doesn't seem well,
but he won't tell me.

25:33.115 --> 25:35.743
Some people have a hard time

25:35.826 --> 25:38.245
sharing things when they care
about someone deeply.

25:40.372 --> 25:41.874
I can guarantee you

25:42.416 --> 25:46.336
that when Chan
really has to tell you something,

25:46.420 --> 25:48.047
he'll tell you honestly

25:48.922 --> 25:50.466
without hiding it.

25:50.549 --> 25:51.675
[♪ heartwarming music playing]

25:51.759 --> 25:55.345
So just trust him
and wait patiently for that moment.

25:57.598 --> 25:58.599
All right.

26:00.392 --> 26:01.393
Mmm.

26:05.022 --> 26:06.774
I startled you in Chuncheon, didn't I?

26:07.357 --> 26:09.985
I was startled too and acted like a child.

26:10.069 --> 26:11.070
I'm sorry.

26:11.153 --> 26:13.739
But you don't have to worry.

26:14.698 --> 26:16.325
I already planned everything.

26:16.408 --> 26:18.827
What plan? To disappear on your own?

26:20.662 --> 26:22.164
Your checkup's tomorrow, right?

26:23.373 --> 26:25.542
You have to take me with you.

26:26.418 --> 26:28.837
How did you know the date?

26:28.921 --> 26:30.464
I met Yougyum.

26:30.547 --> 26:34.468
He told me about the necklace
and how he's the only one who knows.

26:34.551 --> 26:35.928
[chuckles softly]

26:36.720 --> 26:37.888
I see.

26:37.971 --> 26:41.600
But I'm not a child, you know.

26:41.683 --> 26:43.936
-I can go by myself--
-Nabong.

26:45.062 --> 26:47.981
You don't have to act tough
in front of me.

26:50.067 --> 26:51.110
I told you,

26:52.444 --> 26:54.446
I won't let you be alone.

26:56.156 --> 26:57.574
[chuckles]

26:58.784 --> 26:59.952
I guess this is why

27:01.453 --> 27:02.955
we met after 50 years.

27:04.706 --> 27:07.626
You have no one to rely on,
and have so many things to protect.

27:10.379 --> 27:11.588
I'll protect you,

27:13.298 --> 27:14.383
so you can rely on me.

27:15.384 --> 27:17.052
I'll stay by your side.

27:22.766 --> 27:23.767
[sighs softly]

27:23.851 --> 27:24.852
[♪ music ends]

27:31.483 --> 27:32.568
Hmm?

27:35.112 --> 27:37.239
-What is all this?
-[cellphone vibrates]

27:40.075 --> 27:42.703
[Nana] You have to handle
everything on the desk in my place.

27:42.786 --> 27:43.829
Finish them by today.

27:43.912 --> 27:46.456
-[sighs]
-[line connects, rings]

27:46.540 --> 27:48.000
Hello? Ms. Kim--

27:48.083 --> 27:50.961
[Nana] Among the 12 SS candidate outfits,
the six I picked are fixed.

27:51.044 --> 27:53.088
Pick the other six.

27:53.171 --> 27:56.633
Submit a report on which to pick
and the reasons by today.

27:56.717 --> 27:58.135
What? But--

27:58.218 --> 28:00.345
You saw the pigment samples
yesterday, right?

28:00.429 --> 28:03.348
Organize the differences in color
and decide which one to go with.

28:03.432 --> 28:05.976
And the differences by fabric.
Send it by today.

28:06.059 --> 28:07.728
[sighs] Wait, Ms. Kim. I--

28:07.811 --> 28:10.689
I received two drafts
of the press kit for Paris.

28:10.772 --> 28:13.567
Choose the one that suits our image
and give it to Mr. Yeon.

28:13.650 --> 28:16.528
I have work outside the office,
so I won't be there today.

28:16.612 --> 28:19.031
Finish everything by today
and send it to me by email.

28:19.114 --> 28:22.159
-All of that by today?
-Are you saying you can't?

28:22.242 --> 28:23.994
Did you forget?
I told you to take my workload.

28:24.077 --> 28:25.579
-[sighs] But still, this is…
-[line disconnects]

28:29.249 --> 28:30.334
[sighs heavily]

28:31.209 --> 28:32.294
Mr. Park!

28:36.798 --> 28:37.799
[sighs]

28:40.052 --> 28:42.971
Hmm? [inhales sharply]
He didn't mention anything.

28:44.598 --> 28:45.599
Genius.

28:47.726 --> 28:50.145
Do you know where Mr. Park went?

28:51.271 --> 28:52.272
Hmm?

28:53.398 --> 28:55.233
[inhales sharply] Where did he go?

28:57.486 --> 29:01.073
Ms. Kim, can you confirm the materials…

29:01.698 --> 29:02.699
Ah…

29:02.783 --> 29:04.451
Right, she's at a meeting.

29:04.534 --> 29:05.577
[in English] Okay.

29:06.703 --> 29:08.830
-[objects clatter]
-[gasps]

29:08.914 --> 29:11.708
[in Korean] I can't believe this.
Hayeong, you klutz.

29:14.503 --> 29:15.545
Goodness.

29:16.296 --> 29:17.297
What is this?

29:20.550 --> 29:23.053
DON'T CAUSE TROUBLE FOR MY GRANDDAUGHTERS
I'M STILL OKAY

29:23.136 --> 29:24.972
KEEP GLASSES IN FRONT OF THE MONITOR

29:25.055 --> 29:27.015
DON'T TAKE OFF YOUGYUM'S NECKLACE!

29:27.099 --> 29:28.642
[♪ intriguing music playing]

29:29.851 --> 29:32.479
"Noble Life Center"?

29:40.445 --> 29:42.406
NOBLE LIFE CENTER
COUNSELING CENTER

29:46.994 --> 29:48.245
[automation] Secure retirement.

29:48.328 --> 29:51.498
This is the Noble Life Center,
Korea's premium senior care center.

29:52.207 --> 29:54.584
[staff] Hello, this is Noble Life Center.

29:55.711 --> 29:57.629
I…

29:59.381 --> 30:00.382
[hesitates] I mean,

30:01.925 --> 30:02.926
I wanted

30:03.760 --> 30:07.347
to check my reservation.

30:07.431 --> 30:08.598
[staff] What is your name?

30:10.851 --> 30:14.187
I'm Kim Nabong's guardian.

30:14.271 --> 30:15.814
[staff] Right, Kim Nabong.

30:15.897 --> 30:18.483
She's still set to move in
at the end of June, right?

30:19.234 --> 30:21.111
You wanted a single room

30:21.194 --> 30:23.655
and signed up for the specialized
dementia care, right?

30:23.739 --> 30:26.408
CLOSET KEY, JEWELRY BOX

30:27.325 --> 30:28.994
"Closet key, jewelry box…"

30:42.174 --> 30:44.634
[♪ music fades]

30:44.718 --> 30:46.887
[Haran] I really don't need lunch.

30:46.970 --> 30:49.848
[exclaims softly]
When do I finish all of this?

30:55.353 --> 30:56.605
Hayeong.

30:59.775 --> 31:01.068
What is it?

31:01.151 --> 31:03.028
What's wrong? Huh?

31:04.112 --> 31:06.031
[sniffles] What do we do?

31:06.782 --> 31:08.992
[sobbing] What do we do about Grandma?

31:09.576 --> 31:11.870
What about Grandma? What's going on?

31:11.953 --> 31:13.955
[♪ somber music playing]

31:16.333 --> 31:17.542
[stutters] What is this?

31:23.006 --> 31:25.634
NOBLE LIFE CENTER
CALL TO CONFIRM RESERVATION ON THE 17TH!

31:30.680 --> 31:32.349
[Hadam panting]

31:33.141 --> 31:35.852
What do you mean?
Why would she go to a care center?

31:37.187 --> 31:40.857
I know you're just playing a joke
since my CSAT is over.

31:40.941 --> 31:43.276
-Hadam.
-That doesn't make any sense.

31:44.069 --> 31:45.320
Why would Grandma…

31:45.862 --> 31:48.490
[yells] Why would she go there?
[breathing heavily]

31:48.573 --> 31:51.785
[sighs] I think she was trying
to leave quietly.

31:53.745 --> 31:55.455
[Hayeong] She must have been planning it

31:56.206 --> 31:58.083
for quite a long time.

32:02.587 --> 32:04.548
[♪ music fades]

32:13.223 --> 32:15.225
[♪ heartwarming music playing]

32:27.154 --> 32:28.738
This was in here.

32:41.293 --> 32:43.211
[Nana] To my beloved granddaughters.

32:43.795 --> 32:47.465
Bonjour, my beautiful granddaughters
who took after me.

32:47.549 --> 32:49.593
By the time you've opened this,

32:49.676 --> 32:52.470
I'll probably be having champagne

32:52.554 --> 32:54.556
on a plane to southern France.

32:55.640 --> 32:57.017
[med tech] Don't move, ma'am.

32:57.100 --> 32:59.352
[Nana] Don't be too upset.

32:59.978 --> 33:04.024
I want to reward myself
for working hard all these years.

33:04.107 --> 33:05.942
So I'm really happy.

33:06.026 --> 33:08.445
-[nurse] Please curl your back.
-[Nana] Oh.

33:08.528 --> 33:11.615
[Nana] And don't try to visit me.

33:11.698 --> 33:13.992
I had such a hard time in my 20s

33:14.075 --> 33:16.411
attending fashion school
with a baby on my back.

33:16.494 --> 33:18.371
And I didn't get to try so many things

33:18.955 --> 33:21.791
because I had no money or time.

33:22.292 --> 33:26.713
I'm going to be extremely busy
doing everything I couldn't do back then.

33:27.631 --> 33:28.924
So please…

33:29.007 --> 33:30.217
-[nurse] Ms. Kim Nabong.
-Yes.

33:30.300 --> 33:32.761
-[Nana] Let me enjoy my life here.
-Head to the next room.

33:32.844 --> 33:37.015
[Nana] Ah. And as for those
wedding gowns…

33:37.682 --> 33:39.976
[♪ music continues]

33:46.775 --> 33:51.238
Your grandma's the famous Kim Nana,

33:51.321 --> 33:54.366
so letting you wear wedding gowns
made by someone else?

33:54.866 --> 33:56.159
[in English] Oh, no.

33:56.243 --> 33:57.869
[in Korean] I can never let that happen.

33:59.871 --> 34:02.916
I thought I'd be too busy
having fun in France

34:02.999 --> 34:04.834
to make any clothes,

34:04.918 --> 34:06.253
so I made them in advance.

34:07.003 --> 34:10.340
I just made them easily in my spare time.

34:12.801 --> 34:15.428
Let's meet again someday

34:15.512 --> 34:17.806
after shining in each of our places.

34:18.515 --> 34:22.936
I'll be rooting for your glorious lives
from far away.

34:23.728 --> 34:24.813
Haran,

34:24.896 --> 34:26.481
Hayeong,

34:27.315 --> 34:28.400
Hadam.

34:33.029 --> 34:35.240
My life was a brilliant shade of rose

34:35.907 --> 34:40.287
because you three were my granddaughters.

34:41.621 --> 34:42.622
Take care.

34:43.123 --> 34:44.124
[in French] Au revoir.

34:45.166 --> 34:46.167
Ah.

34:46.251 --> 34:50.755
[in Korean] I hate saying cheesy things,
but I'm the type to say things I need to.

34:50.839 --> 34:52.048
[♪ music ends]

34:52.132 --> 34:53.133
I love you,

34:53.800 --> 34:55.760
my dear granddaughters.

34:58.179 --> 34:59.389
[Hadam] Why…

34:59.889 --> 35:00.890
[Haran sighs]

35:00.974 --> 35:03.018
She has three granddaughters.

35:04.269 --> 35:05.437
Why would she…

35:05.520 --> 35:07.188
It's weird that she's at a meeting.

35:08.356 --> 35:09.608
Where is she right now?

35:10.775 --> 35:12.319
She hasn't left already, has she?

35:13.945 --> 35:14.946
[sighs heavily]

35:21.494 --> 35:24.706
SECRET WITH YOUGYUM
DON'T TAKE OFF YOUGYUM'S NECKLACE!

35:24.789 --> 35:25.999
[♪ mysterious music playing]

35:26.082 --> 35:28.335
Why don't you spend some time
with your grandma--

35:28.418 --> 35:30.795
Why are you suddenly
bringing up my grandma?

35:30.879 --> 35:31.880
What?

35:32.839 --> 35:33.840
Oh…

35:33.923 --> 35:36.885
Why was your tumbler
in my grandma's study?

35:36.968 --> 35:38.678
I ran into her a while ago in the park.

35:38.762 --> 35:40.889
You know she wouldn't do such a thing.

35:48.146 --> 35:51.858
[breath trembling] Cha Yougyum.
You knew about Grandma, didn't you?

35:52.484 --> 35:53.735
Where is she right now?

35:53.818 --> 35:57.155
[yelling] I already know everything!
Just tell me! [breathing heavily]

35:58.406 --> 36:00.659
[Yougyum] She's getting a checkup today.

36:07.957 --> 36:08.958
Over there.

36:09.042 --> 36:10.960
NEUROLOGY CENTER

36:15.131 --> 36:16.925
-[Manjae] Oh.
-Hey, Manjae.

36:17.008 --> 36:18.718
-That took a while, didn't it?
-[Manjae] Goodness.

36:18.843 --> 36:20.053
You did great.

36:20.136 --> 36:21.429
-Are you okay?
-[Nana] Yes.

36:21.513 --> 36:23.515
[♪ mellow music playing]

36:27.894 --> 36:29.270
[sighs]

36:29.354 --> 36:30.730
How can you…

36:30.814 --> 36:32.899
Of all people, how can you do this to me?

36:32.982 --> 36:34.526
Why are you--

36:34.609 --> 36:36.444
You should take some of my workload.

36:36.528 --> 36:38.238
Let me get some rest, too.

36:38.321 --> 36:40.782
He's not keeping it from you.
He probably can't.

36:40.865 --> 36:43.576
He probably doesn't want
to burden you with his pain.

36:43.660 --> 36:46.287
He cares more about protecting you
than his own pain.

36:47.497 --> 36:48.498
[sighs]

36:52.711 --> 36:53.920
[Hayeong] A meeting?

36:54.003 --> 36:55.422
And what's this…

36:55.505 --> 36:56.506
I'll do it.

37:02.512 --> 37:03.596
[Hadam] What was that, Grandma?

37:03.680 --> 37:05.932
You didn't even look at him
and didn't say a word.

37:06.015 --> 37:08.184
He left because
you made him uncomfortable.

37:08.268 --> 37:11.271
Did Grandma summon you
and threaten you or something?

37:11.855 --> 37:14.274
[breathes deeply, sighs]

37:14.816 --> 37:16.735
[♪ music continues]

37:23.533 --> 37:25.493
DON'T CAUSE TROUBLE FOR MY GRANDDAUGHTERS

37:38.465 --> 37:39.466
[Hadam] Grandma.

37:47.974 --> 37:49.100
[Nana] I'm okay.

37:49.684 --> 37:50.685
It's all right.

37:53.938 --> 37:56.316
[nurse] Ms. Kim Nabong.
Please go to the next room.

37:56.399 --> 37:57.442
[Manjae] Okay.

37:58.735 --> 38:00.028
I'll be back.

38:00.111 --> 38:01.196
[Manjae] Let's go.

38:02.655 --> 38:04.783
-[Haran sighs worriedly]
-[Manjae mumbles]

38:07.076 --> 38:08.119
[sighs]

38:10.914 --> 38:13.249
-[Nana sniffles]
-[Manjae] You've a lot of granddaughters.

38:13.333 --> 38:14.751
All right.

38:14.834 --> 38:15.835
See you in a bit.

38:18.922 --> 38:20.131
[Hayeong sighs wearily]

38:28.056 --> 38:29.057
[sighs heavily]

38:29.140 --> 38:31.142
[♪ music ends]

38:31.851 --> 38:35.730
Make sure to keep it dry,
and tell me if it's too tight.

38:35.814 --> 38:37.065
Okay. Thank you.

38:38.983 --> 38:39.984
[Changmo] Are you okay?

38:40.068 --> 38:41.569
[grunts] I'm fine.

38:42.737 --> 38:44.906
You need some vitamins.
I'll peel these for you.

38:44.989 --> 38:47.283
-It's fine, I'll do it.
-Mmm-mmm.

38:47.367 --> 38:49.619
-Ah…
-[yells] Cha Yougyum!

38:50.370 --> 38:51.371
[sighs]

38:52.330 --> 38:53.331
Bye.

38:57.126 --> 38:58.127
Hadam…

39:00.880 --> 39:03.258
I'm sorry I didn't tell you
about your grandma.

39:03.341 --> 39:05.009
She said…

39:08.721 --> 39:10.765
Thank you, Yougyum. [sobbing]

39:10.849 --> 39:11.850
[♪ mellow music playing]

39:11.933 --> 39:13.351
Thank you so much.

39:14.477 --> 39:17.564
[Manjae]
Yougyum has been taking care of her.

39:17.647 --> 39:19.357
Without the necklace he gave her,

39:19.440 --> 39:22.277
I would've lost her in Chuncheon.

39:23.403 --> 39:26.948
It must have been tough
keeping that secret on his own.

39:27.657 --> 39:30.243
She would've had a hard time on her own.

39:32.036 --> 39:33.037
Thank you

39:33.788 --> 39:35.456
for taking care of her.

39:41.838 --> 39:43.172
Sorry, I didn't tell you.

39:43.715 --> 39:45.133
You must've been shocked.

39:46.551 --> 39:47.552
Thank you.

39:48.887 --> 39:51.306
Thank you so, so much, Yougyum.

39:55.351 --> 39:57.979
Let's go see her.

39:59.230 --> 40:01.232
[♪ music ends]

40:01.316 --> 40:03.318
[panting]

40:19.292 --> 40:20.293
[Taeseok] I didn't know.

40:22.545 --> 40:24.505
I should've known,

40:26.174 --> 40:27.175
but I didn't.

40:27.842 --> 40:28.843
Why?

40:29.385 --> 40:31.429
How could you not know?

40:32.180 --> 40:34.641
It was you of all people.

40:34.724 --> 40:36.225
You said she was your savior,

40:37.060 --> 40:38.686
and you promised to take care of her.

40:38.770 --> 40:41.105
You were always by her side.
How could you not know?

40:41.189 --> 40:42.982
[♪ melancholic music playing]

40:43.066 --> 40:45.735
When I asked if anything happened
in Seongsu-dong,

40:46.569 --> 40:47.862
why did you hide it from me?

40:48.738 --> 40:50.990
No, if you weren't going to tell me,

40:51.074 --> 40:53.201
shouldn't you have
looked into it more, at least?

40:53.284 --> 40:55.161
If you'd found out then…

40:56.079 --> 40:57.080
I'm sorry.

40:58.247 --> 40:59.248
[Hayeong] No.

41:00.083 --> 41:01.501
Pretend you didn't hear that.

41:02.460 --> 41:03.878
What I just said

41:04.671 --> 41:06.839
is actually what I want to say to myself.

41:09.092 --> 41:11.302
I know it's not your fault,

41:11.886 --> 41:15.974
but I feel so pathetic and stupid.

41:17.475 --> 41:19.727
So I don't know what to do.

41:20.979 --> 41:23.189
I should've known.

41:24.399 --> 41:25.400
I'm sorry…

41:26.275 --> 41:27.527
I yelled at you.

41:36.619 --> 41:37.620
[breath trembling]

41:38.746 --> 41:39.789
Sorry.

41:39.872 --> 41:40.873
[♪ music ends]

41:41.791 --> 41:43.793
[line connects, rings]

41:46.587 --> 41:47.755
He's not picking up.

41:48.756 --> 41:50.550
Mr. Park, where are you?

41:50.633 --> 41:53.386
Customers are coming in,
asking why you're closed today.

41:55.763 --> 41:56.764
The hospital?

41:58.850 --> 42:00.184
Then what about…

42:00.268 --> 42:02.437
What about Ms. Song?

42:03.062 --> 42:06.149
[doctor] The MRI shows
normal intracranial pressure,

42:06.232 --> 42:09.235
but the ventricles
are significantly enlarged.

42:09.318 --> 42:11.904
We also ran a cerebrospinal fluid test
to double-check,

42:11.988 --> 42:13.531
and the results show…

42:16.159 --> 42:17.410
that it's not dementia.

42:18.619 --> 42:20.163
-Really?
-[all sigh in relief]

42:20.246 --> 42:21.497
[Hayeong whispers] That's such a relief.

42:21.581 --> 42:25.460
But we suspect
normal pressure hydrocephalus.

42:25.543 --> 42:27.128
Hydrocephalus?

42:27.211 --> 42:30.006
It occurs when cerebrospinal fluid
isn't properly absorbed,

42:30.089 --> 42:33.843
leading to symptoms like memory loss
and problems with walking.

42:33.926 --> 42:36.804
The symptoms are similar,
so some mistake it for dementia.

42:36.888 --> 42:38.139
I see.

42:38.222 --> 42:41.059
Have you had any problems
with walking recently?

42:42.185 --> 42:44.937
-I don't think I've seen…
-I'm not sure…

42:45.438 --> 42:46.564
-[Yougyum exclaims] Oh!
-[Manjae] Oh gosh.

42:46.647 --> 42:50.276
She did. Last time,
you had bruises on your legs.

42:50.359 --> 42:52.487
Huh? Did you hit your leg somewhere?

42:52.570 --> 42:55.323
It's fine. I just fell.
My legs suddenly wouldn't listen.

42:56.074 --> 42:58.493
[doctor] Patients usually show a response
within 24 hours,

42:58.576 --> 43:01.204
even within 10 hours
after draining the cerebrospinal fluid.

43:01.287 --> 43:03.748
We'll be able to confirm this
after the gait test.

43:03.831 --> 43:06.084
So let's see
how much improvement there is.

43:06.876 --> 43:09.545
You can see how you sometimes
had narrower strides

43:09.629 --> 43:12.173
and dragged your feet
in the morning, right?

43:12.256 --> 43:14.801
But it improved significantly
after draining the fluid.

43:15.843 --> 43:18.805
The tap test confirms
normal pressure hydrocephalus.

43:18.888 --> 43:22.433
[inhales sharply] She can get better
with treatment, right?

43:22.517 --> 43:24.310
With successful surgery,
she should improve.

43:24.393 --> 43:25.812
[Manjae] All right.

43:25.895 --> 43:28.231
We'll create a small opening in the skull

43:28.314 --> 43:31.150
and insert a thin tube called a shunt
into the ventricle

43:31.234 --> 43:34.737
to drain excess cerebrospinal fluid
into the abdomen.

43:34.821 --> 43:36.322
Ah…

43:36.405 --> 43:39.575
[doctor] Given your age, I suggest
getting hospitalized a few days in advance

43:39.659 --> 43:41.327
to run some basic tests first.

43:41.994 --> 43:43.412
Proceed with the admission,

43:43.496 --> 43:46.749
and we'll set the surgery date
based on your condition.

43:46.833 --> 43:48.292
[♪ mellow music playing]

43:48.376 --> 43:50.795
The admission's done already?

43:50.878 --> 43:55.341
Yes, a tall man in a suit
came and finished the process.

43:55.424 --> 43:56.926
He even paid the fees.

43:57.593 --> 43:58.803
[sighs]

44:00.763 --> 44:01.848
[Hayeong] Mr. Yeon.

44:01.931 --> 44:04.225
[panting]

44:25.538 --> 44:27.540
[♪ music fades]

44:28.124 --> 44:29.167
Cha Yougyum.

44:29.250 --> 44:30.251
Yes, Ms. Kim.

44:30.334 --> 44:34.172
You're an athlete.
Go take care of your own condition.

44:34.255 --> 44:35.423
You need to recover.

44:35.506 --> 44:37.341
-Song Hadam.
-Yes?

44:37.967 --> 44:39.260
You said you'd help him.

44:39.760 --> 44:41.554
Stay right by his side.

44:42.555 --> 44:43.598
And…

44:44.724 --> 44:46.225
Song Haran, Song Hayeong.

44:46.309 --> 44:50.271
No, Lead Designer Song,
Designer Song Hayeong.

44:50.354 --> 44:55.026
If anything at my company
goes wrong while I'm away,

44:55.109 --> 44:56.444
I'm kicking all of you out.

44:56.527 --> 44:58.237
So focus on work from now on.

44:58.321 --> 45:00.489
Don't even think about coming here.

45:00.573 --> 45:01.866
-But…
-[Manjae claps]

45:02.450 --> 45:03.451
[in English] Okay.

45:03.534 --> 45:06.204
[in Korean] I'll be taking care of her
from now on,

45:06.287 --> 45:09.665
so you youngsters
go and focus on your own stuff.

45:09.749 --> 45:12.043
We'll take turns coming here.
You have your coffee shop.

45:12.126 --> 45:13.127
[Manjae] Mmm-mmm.

45:13.211 --> 45:15.504
SHIM is temporarily closed
until she gets surgery

45:15.588 --> 45:18.341
and recovers well.

45:18.424 --> 45:19.884
I'll think of this as winter vacation

45:19.967 --> 45:23.262
and enjoy my time here with my old friend.

45:23.346 --> 45:24.472
[chuckles]

45:24.555 --> 45:27.016
All right. Everyone, stop bothering us.

45:28.100 --> 45:30.645
But where did Mr. Yeon go?

45:30.728 --> 45:33.105
-I thought I saw him in the hallway.
-[Haran] Oh.

45:33.189 --> 45:35.191
He'll probably be busy
taking care of things

45:35.274 --> 45:36.817
in Grandma's place.

45:40.279 --> 45:42.281
[breathing heavily]

45:46.953 --> 45:47.995
Oh?

45:50.289 --> 45:51.290
[♪ heartwarming music playing]

45:51.374 --> 45:53.876
I'm sorry, I took so long.

45:54.543 --> 45:55.878
How did you know?

45:55.962 --> 45:58.589
I heard from Mr. Park just a while ago.

45:58.673 --> 46:01.300
I'm sure her surgery will go well.

46:01.384 --> 46:02.551
[sighs]

46:02.635 --> 46:08.182
I wish the people I love won't feel pain,
physically or mentally.

46:08.766 --> 46:10.476
I'm sure she'll overcome this.

46:10.559 --> 46:12.436
So don't get too scared.

46:12.520 --> 46:13.854
Everything will be all right.

46:14.397 --> 46:18.276
[sighs] Sorry, but can we stay like this
for 10 more seconds?

46:18.359 --> 46:21.821
We can stay like this for 10 minutes
or even 10 hours.

46:22.613 --> 46:25.157
[sighs] Sorry,
I didn't contact you sooner.

46:25.241 --> 46:26.492
Things were so hectic.

46:27.243 --> 46:28.244
Oh?

46:29.495 --> 46:31.622
I'll be upset if you feel sorry over this.

46:31.706 --> 46:33.332
[chuckles softly]

46:33.416 --> 46:34.709
You must've missed lunch.

46:35.501 --> 46:37.044
Wait here, I'll get you something.

46:37.128 --> 46:41.132
Then can I just get some coffee?
I don't think I can eat anything.

46:41.215 --> 46:43.009
All right. Hang on.

46:43.592 --> 46:46.637
[inhales sharply]
Why are you dressed so lightly?

46:48.431 --> 46:51.726
This cardigan is really valuable to me,

46:51.809 --> 46:54.103
so I don't usually lend it to anyone.

46:54.186 --> 46:56.188
But I'll let you wear it just this once.

47:00.484 --> 47:01.485
Don't ruin it.

47:05.364 --> 47:07.575
[♪ music fades]

47:10.953 --> 47:12.163
[footsteps approaching]

47:12.246 --> 47:13.247
[Sujin] We meet again.

47:14.457 --> 47:16.042
Oh. Hello.

47:16.625 --> 47:19.920
My grandma's getting hospitalized here
for a few days.

47:20.004 --> 47:21.464
Ah. Really?

47:22.006 --> 47:25.634
Oh, um… I accidentally took
one of your bracelet charms.

47:25.718 --> 47:27.887
I'll give it back to you
when I visit tomorrow.

47:27.970 --> 47:30.389
Really? I was wondering
where that charm went.

47:30.473 --> 47:32.808
That's great. But…

47:33.351 --> 47:35.144
the man who was with you last time…

47:36.979 --> 47:38.356
Is he your boyfriend?

47:39.190 --> 47:40.691
Yes. Why do you ask?

47:40.775 --> 47:42.151
You looked good together.

47:42.902 --> 47:45.988
He reminded me of someone I used to know.

47:46.072 --> 47:47.782
-Ah. [chuckles softly]
-[♪ suspenseful music playing]

47:48.366 --> 47:50.826
Oh… You're a neurology doctor.

47:51.702 --> 47:54.288
My grandmother's getting surgery
for hydrocephalus.

47:54.372 --> 47:55.956
Please take good care of her.

47:56.040 --> 47:58.959
I'm only visiting, so I'm not authorized
to treat patients directly.

48:01.545 --> 48:02.755
I came from Boston.

48:03.547 --> 48:04.548
[Haran] Oh.

48:05.091 --> 48:06.384
I see.

48:06.467 --> 48:08.219
The neurosurgeons
will take good care of her.

48:08.302 --> 48:11.430
The neurology department
will see the results, so I'll check.

48:12.014 --> 48:13.349
And my bracelet…

48:14.058 --> 48:15.476
I was worried

48:16.352 --> 48:19.146
about the gap in my bracelet.

48:19.772 --> 48:22.108
I'm glad you'll give it back to me.

48:22.191 --> 48:24.193
-I'll see you tomorrow.
-All right.

48:25.319 --> 48:26.320
Bye.

48:29.865 --> 48:30.908
You're back.

48:32.451 --> 48:34.870
[cellphone vibrating]

48:36.705 --> 48:38.165
Yes, Mr. Park.

48:38.249 --> 48:40.709
Oh, I met Mr. Seonu in the lobby.

48:40.793 --> 48:42.128
Really?

48:42.795 --> 48:43.796
Okay.

48:43.879 --> 48:47.466
Grandma said
she wants to talk to you alone.

48:47.550 --> 48:48.884
Is that okay?

48:48.968 --> 48:51.887
-If you feel uncomfortable…
-[chuckles softly] No, it's fine.

48:53.264 --> 48:55.266
[♪ music fades]

48:55.891 --> 48:58.727
I should have put more thought
into what you said that day.

48:58.811 --> 49:00.438
I'm sorry, Ms. Kim.

49:00.521 --> 49:01.856
"That day"?

49:01.939 --> 49:04.108
Thanks to you,
I'll be able to leave in peace.

49:04.191 --> 49:05.568
Are you going somewhere?

49:06.694 --> 49:09.697
I'm planning to stay in France
after I retire.

49:12.908 --> 49:15.035
I hid this on purpose.

49:15.661 --> 49:17.329
How could you have known?

49:19.498 --> 49:20.499
Are you all right?

49:21.083 --> 49:22.460
I'm fine.

49:24.086 --> 49:25.087
But…

49:25.629 --> 49:27.423
I'd like to ask you the same thing.

49:27.506 --> 49:28.924
I heard about your head.

49:30.134 --> 49:31.469
Are you sure you're okay?

49:33.012 --> 49:34.013
I'm fine.

49:34.930 --> 49:35.973
No,

49:36.056 --> 49:38.225
I'm going to make sure I'm fine

49:38.893 --> 49:41.145
so I can stay by Ms. Song's side.

49:42.021 --> 49:44.148
My head, and everything else…

49:46.692 --> 49:48.027
I'm going to make it all okay.

49:48.110 --> 49:50.112
[♪ mellow music playing]

49:50.863 --> 49:51.864
Haran cares…

49:53.365 --> 49:55.117
for you a lot.

49:55.201 --> 49:58.287
It actually surprised me
how sincere she is about you.

49:58.913 --> 50:01.999
And she seems to be
thinking of a future with you.

50:03.250 --> 50:06.295
I know, and I feel the same way.

50:06.378 --> 50:07.755
[Nana] I want to see you two

50:09.173 --> 50:11.634
getting along well for as long as I can.

50:12.885 --> 50:16.347
At least for Haran's sake and your sake,

50:17.848 --> 50:19.225
make sure you're okay.

50:23.062 --> 50:24.063
I will.

50:27.691 --> 50:29.318
Thanks for coming.

50:29.401 --> 50:31.987
Oh. When's your checkup again?

50:32.071 --> 50:33.072
Next week.

50:33.155 --> 50:35.282
It'll be fine, so don't worry about me.

50:35.366 --> 50:36.700
Take good care of Ms. Kim.

50:37.284 --> 50:38.285
I'll get going now.

50:38.369 --> 50:40.037
-Right, your cardigan.
-Ah…

50:41.038 --> 50:42.706
Keep it on. You'll catch a cold.

50:45.209 --> 50:46.418
Don't worry.

50:50.422 --> 50:51.882
Grandma was right.

50:53.008 --> 50:56.637
Having just one person to lean on

50:56.720 --> 50:58.097
will help you stay strong.

51:00.182 --> 51:02.142
[inhales sharply, exclaims boastfully]

51:02.226 --> 51:04.853
I do have a pretty broad back.

51:04.937 --> 51:06.188
When did you notice?

51:06.272 --> 51:08.524
Should I leave my back here
for you to lean on?

51:08.607 --> 51:09.608
[chuckles softly]

51:10.943 --> 51:13.529
-Go. [chuckling]
-Okay. I'll go now.

51:13.612 --> 51:14.613
Bye.

51:18.158 --> 51:19.243
Head back inside.

51:22.913 --> 51:24.915
[footsteps receding]

51:25.541 --> 51:26.542
[sighs]

51:39.513 --> 51:40.514
Let me talk to you.

51:41.807 --> 51:43.225
What do you think you're doing?

51:43.309 --> 51:44.935
Stop messing with her.

51:45.019 --> 51:46.687
The thing you wanted to protect…

51:48.230 --> 51:49.231
was her?

51:49.940 --> 51:52.318
Are you worried you'll lose her
if I say something?

51:53.319 --> 51:54.570
Does she know

51:54.653 --> 51:58.073
that you went to the same school
as Hyeokchan and were his roommate?

51:58.157 --> 51:59.158
Does she know who you are?

52:00.492 --> 52:03.203
Hyeokchan's dead, but you're alive,

52:03.287 --> 52:05.873
and the person you want to protect
is his old girlfriend?

52:07.041 --> 52:08.083
That's funny.

52:08.167 --> 52:09.168
Since when?

52:09.251 --> 52:10.919
Did you have feelings for her then?

52:11.003 --> 52:12.963
You must've jumped at the chance
when he died.

52:13.047 --> 52:14.757
Don't say it like that.

52:14.840 --> 52:16.216
That's not the case.

52:17.259 --> 52:20.262
She's going through a hard time right now.

52:20.888 --> 52:23.182
Don't say things that…

52:24.224 --> 52:25.601
will only dig up old wounds.

52:25.684 --> 52:27.102
Please.

52:27.186 --> 52:29.355
Why should I do that for you?

52:30.356 --> 52:31.357
[scoffs]

52:32.524 --> 52:33.692
I remembered something.

52:34.568 --> 52:36.153
The day that the waste container fell,

52:37.529 --> 52:39.281
you were in the lab as well.

52:39.365 --> 52:40.949
And you were shouting at him to stop.

52:41.033 --> 52:43.077
[♪ tense music playing]

52:44.078 --> 52:47.206
I don't have the time
to answer all your questions.

52:47.289 --> 52:49.875
Why was the waste container
next to Hyeokchan?

52:52.127 --> 52:54.171
The day Hyeokchan's lip was busted…

52:54.254 --> 52:55.339
Was that day

52:56.048 --> 52:58.008
the day of the accident?

52:59.218 --> 53:02.012
I didn't have any memories
of that day until now,

53:02.096 --> 53:04.014
but it feels like it's from that day.

53:04.098 --> 53:08.018
Tell me what happened in the lab that day.

53:09.395 --> 53:10.396
You know what happened.

53:12.106 --> 53:14.692
You can't tell Haran the truth.

53:14.775 --> 53:16.026
No, you're not telling her.

53:16.110 --> 53:18.737
So why are you so obsessed
with finding out what happened?

53:18.821 --> 53:21.198
If everyone involved
has the right to know,

53:21.281 --> 53:24.868
shouldn't Haran also know
that you're fake?

53:25.828 --> 53:27.287
I'm going to tell her.

53:27.371 --> 53:29.873
-But right now--
-If you go and tell her first,

53:29.957 --> 53:32.668
then I might think about telling you, too.

53:40.759 --> 53:41.844
Please.

53:41.927 --> 53:43.971
Stop asking me strange questions.

53:44.763 --> 53:46.056
If you provoke me,

53:46.140 --> 53:49.685
even I don't know
what I'll end up telling her.

53:57.651 --> 53:58.777
[Chan] Hey, Kang Hyeokchan.

53:59.570 --> 54:01.113
I have to tell you something.

54:01.196 --> 54:04.616
I've been chatting with your girlfriend.

54:04.700 --> 54:06.452
She thinks she's been talking to you.

54:07.035 --> 54:08.203
You were pretending to be me?

54:08.287 --> 54:09.788
Do you have any idea what you've done?

54:09.872 --> 54:11.123
[♪ music ends]

54:11.206 --> 54:13.125
-I'm sorry.
-[Sujin] Did you have feelings for her?

54:13.208 --> 54:14.835
You must've jumped at the chance.

54:14.918 --> 54:17.296
Shouldn't Haran also know
that you're fake?

54:18.130 --> 54:20.174
[panting]

54:22.801 --> 54:24.094
[Chan] I told him…

54:24.678 --> 54:25.929
I told Hyeokchan everything.

54:26.764 --> 54:27.765
But…

54:29.099 --> 54:31.059
what happened after that?

54:35.856 --> 54:37.858
[continues panting]

54:46.116 --> 54:47.868
I'm sorry. It's all my fault.

54:48.744 --> 54:50.037
It's all my fault.

54:51.038 --> 54:52.080
"Fault…"

54:59.171 --> 55:01.048
-[Raemee] Nineteen.
-Nineteen.

55:01.632 --> 55:04.343
-[Raemee] Thirty-one point five.
-Thirty-one point five.

55:04.426 --> 55:06.553
Everyone, let's keep our spirits up.

55:06.637 --> 55:08.430
When Ms. Kim comes back,

55:08.514 --> 55:11.475
we should show her how much we did
to put her mind at ease.

55:11.558 --> 55:13.602
So how about a quick cheer?

55:13.685 --> 55:15.437
No, forget it.

55:16.688 --> 55:18.690
One, two, three.

55:18.774 --> 55:20.025
[all] Let's do this!

55:21.068 --> 55:22.236
[Chan] Let's do this!

55:22.319 --> 55:23.487
Whatever it is.

55:23.570 --> 55:24.571
-Hey.
-It's Chan.

55:24.655 --> 55:26.615
[Raemee] What's the occasion?
There's no meeting today.

55:26.698 --> 55:28.909
We got the additional script,
so I dropped by.

55:28.992 --> 55:32.329
[smacks lips] And since SHIM is closed,
I made these myself.

55:32.412 --> 55:33.455
I can't guarantee the taste.

55:33.539 --> 55:34.873
-Thank you.
-[Seunggyu] Thank you.

55:34.957 --> 55:38.627
But Ms. Song isn't here right now.

55:38.710 --> 55:39.836
Really?

55:39.920 --> 55:42.422
-Where did she go?
-She took the afternoon off.

55:42.506 --> 55:46.218
Even if Ms. Kim told her not to come,
I guess she's pretty worried.

55:46.301 --> 55:47.636
Did she go to the hospital?

55:47.719 --> 55:50.097
No, she said she had to drop by somewhere.

55:50.180 --> 55:52.766
She had to return something to someone.

55:52.849 --> 55:53.850
Oh…

55:54.601 --> 55:55.978
[Sujin] And my bracelet…

55:56.061 --> 55:57.938
I'm glad you'll give it back to me.

55:58.021 --> 55:59.606
I'll see you tomorrow.

55:59.690 --> 56:01.316
[♪ tense music playing]

56:02.067 --> 56:06.530
[navigator] Sunyul National
University Hospital is 1.5 km ahead.

56:10.701 --> 56:13.287
[Sujin] Does she know who you are?

56:16.206 --> 56:17.374
If you provoke me,

56:18.584 --> 56:22.296
even I don't know
what I'll end up telling her.

56:23.589 --> 56:26.174
[♪ music swells]

56:26.258 --> 56:28.010
[panting]

56:30.721 --> 56:32.723
[♪ music continues]

56:39.855 --> 56:43.275
Ah. The last patient's tone
seemed worse than the tremor.

56:43.358 --> 56:45.444
-Let's reduce the dose.
-[doctor] Okay, I'll check.

56:47.863 --> 56:49.239
[♪ music ends]

56:49.906 --> 56:51.283
[Chan panting]

56:57.164 --> 56:58.165
[sighs]

57:02.544 --> 57:04.713
-Oh. Haran.
-[Haran] You're here.

57:04.796 --> 57:07.966
Mr. Seonu's upstairs, right?
I have to give him something.

57:08.050 --> 57:09.718
He just left when I came here.

57:10.302 --> 57:11.678
He said he had to go somewhere.

57:11.762 --> 57:12.763
Oh…

57:13.597 --> 57:16.224
Then can I just leave this in his room?

57:16.308 --> 57:17.809
[Manjae] Sure, that's fine.

57:17.893 --> 57:21.146
I'm heading back to the hospital.
I just came to get my stuff.

57:21.229 --> 57:24.191
Then I'll give you a ride.
I'm heading there, too.

57:24.274 --> 57:26.026
No, it's fine. I called a cab.

57:26.109 --> 57:29.321
I made a lot of coffee
to share with the doctors.

57:29.404 --> 57:31.865
I'll leave one for you.

57:31.948 --> 57:34.951
Take your time drinking this
and meet Chan first.

57:35.035 --> 57:36.536
-Okay.
-[Manjae] He'll be back soon.

57:38.288 --> 57:39.289
Mr. Park.

57:39.998 --> 57:40.999
Yes?

57:41.083 --> 57:43.585
Thank you for taking care of my grandma.

57:44.836 --> 57:46.672
[chuckling] Gosh.

57:47.422 --> 57:49.049
There's no need to thank me.

57:49.132 --> 57:51.134
[♪ heartwarming music playing]

57:55.806 --> 57:58.558
TEMPORARILY CLOSED
SORRY FOR THE INCONVENIENCE

58:04.981 --> 58:07.067
Pardon me.

58:11.488 --> 58:14.658
[cellphone vibrating]

58:14.741 --> 58:16.660
SEONU CHAN

58:17.994 --> 58:18.995
[chuckles]

58:19.746 --> 58:21.665
[cellphone vibrating]

58:26.795 --> 58:27.921
Hey, roomie.

58:29.005 --> 58:30.132
Yes, she's here.

58:30.215 --> 58:32.384
She brought something for you,
so she went upstairs.

58:33.093 --> 58:34.720
Hang on.

58:34.803 --> 58:36.054
No, it's okay.

58:36.138 --> 58:37.764
I'll be there in a few minutes.

58:37.848 --> 58:39.057
-Really?
-[cellphone chimes]

58:39.141 --> 58:41.268
Huh? My cab's here.

58:41.768 --> 58:43.395
I'm going to the hospital,

58:43.895 --> 58:46.106
so take care of Genius for me.

58:48.900 --> 58:50.777
Is there a Post-it? Oh?

58:53.405 --> 58:54.406
[chuckles softly]

59:09.671 --> 59:11.673
[♪ music ends]

59:32.778 --> 59:33.779
Is she upstairs?

59:34.738 --> 59:35.906
Are you here?

59:37.532 --> 59:38.617
Huh?

59:42.579 --> 59:43.747
Hmm?

59:46.750 --> 59:48.084
THANKS FOR THE

59:50.754 --> 59:52.172
[inhales sharply, mumbles]

59:55.300 --> 59:57.511
-[line connects, rings]
-[inhales sharply]

01:00:01.389 --> 01:00:03.391
[line continues ringing]

01:00:06.269 --> 01:00:08.063
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

01:00:20.200 --> 01:00:22.452
[thud echoes]

01:00:22.536 --> 01:00:24.871
KANG HYEOKCHAN, GLASS TUBE, BLOOD
THAT SOUND AGAIN

01:00:34.673 --> 01:00:37.509
KANG HYEOKCHAN HOSPITALIZED, WOMAN
THAT SOUND WAS HER BRACELET

01:00:39.344 --> 01:00:41.513
[Chan] I'll tell her everything

01:00:41.596 --> 01:00:43.056
and apologize to her.

01:00:44.057 --> 01:00:45.433
I want to tell her everything

01:00:45.517 --> 01:00:48.395
and love her as my true self…

01:00:49.980 --> 01:00:50.981
from now on.

01:00:51.857 --> 01:00:52.899
Before it's too late.

01:00:56.444 --> 01:00:57.779
[♪ music continues]

01:00:58.363 --> 01:01:00.365
[breathing heavily]

01:01:12.168 --> 01:01:13.503
Chan.

01:01:13.587 --> 01:01:14.963
Why did you come back?

01:01:15.046 --> 01:01:16.339
Well…

01:01:16.423 --> 01:01:18.967
Did Ms. Song come here?

01:01:19.050 --> 01:01:20.427
Hey, what's gotten into you?

01:01:20.510 --> 01:01:23.138
-We told you she's going to the hospital.
-Ah…

01:01:25.390 --> 01:01:26.391
All right.

01:01:29.185 --> 01:01:33.398
Mr. Park, is Ms. Song
at the hospital right now?

01:01:33.481 --> 01:01:35.275
No, she's not here.

01:01:35.358 --> 01:01:38.069
Did you not see her?

01:01:38.153 --> 01:01:39.195
Oh…

01:01:40.196 --> 01:01:41.573
It's nothing. Never mind.

01:01:54.878 --> 01:01:57.255
-[♪ music fades]
-[Chan pants]

01:01:57.923 --> 01:01:59.799
[♪ somber music playing]

01:01:59.883 --> 01:02:02.010
RAN

01:02:08.224 --> 01:02:09.684
[Chan] Are you home?

01:02:09.768 --> 01:02:11.227
If you're home, come out.

01:02:11.311 --> 01:02:13.355
Let's meet. Let's meet up and talk.

01:02:13.438 --> 01:02:14.856
I'll explain everything.

01:02:33.875 --> 01:02:35.877
[♪ music continues]

01:02:53.728 --> 01:02:55.313
-Hey…
-[Haran] Don't come any closer.

01:03:02.278 --> 01:03:04.447
[♪ music fades]

01:03:04.531 --> 01:03:06.074
Boston Institute of Technology.

01:03:07.617 --> 01:03:09.327
Kang Hyeokchan's roommate.

01:03:10.787 --> 01:03:12.163
Have you really known me

01:03:13.289 --> 01:03:15.000
for seven years?

01:03:21.172 --> 01:03:22.841
-Song Haran.
-Don't say my name.

01:03:24.467 --> 01:03:25.969
[breath trembling]

01:03:26.052 --> 01:03:27.303
Did you have fun

01:03:28.596 --> 01:03:30.223
pretending to be Kang Hyeokchan?

01:03:32.809 --> 01:03:33.810
[breath trembling]

01:03:33.893 --> 01:03:35.895
[♪ emotional song playing]

01:03:41.735 --> 01:03:43.695
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

01:04:07.802 --> 01:04:10.805
[Chan] She found out about everything.

01:04:10.889 --> 01:04:12.557
I didn't have the chance to explain.

01:04:12.640 --> 01:04:14.517
[Haran] If those two facts don't change,

01:04:15.226 --> 01:04:16.311
I won't change, either.

01:04:17.187 --> 01:04:18.813
Don't ever show up in front of me again.

01:04:18.897 --> 01:04:22.150
[Chan] You don't have to look at me
or listen to me. So please,

01:04:22.901 --> 01:04:24.444
just look at this.

01:04:24.527 --> 01:04:26.946
[Hayeong] Haran, you're burning up.

01:04:27.030 --> 01:04:29.657
[Nana] You did a great job so far
working by my side.

01:04:29.741 --> 01:04:31.659
[Hayeong] Haran's gone.

01:04:31.743 --> 01:04:34.162
You're the only one I could ask
where she could be.

01:04:34.245 --> 01:04:36.372
[Chan] I have to go find her.

01:04:36.456 --> 01:04:38.458
It has to be me.

01:04:40.502 --> 01:04:42.504
[♪ song fades]

01:04:42.587 --> 01:04:44.589
[♪ theme music playing]

01:04:50.470 --> 01:04:51.471
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

01:04:51.554 --> 01:04:52.555
Translated by Juyoung Park
